CONTEXT: the sub-band-only fix (3564728f) gated the W44-108 low-colour SUB-band
(d in [2.0, 3.5)) on mask1x1_p25 >= 95 but left the d>=3.5 MAIN band unguarded.
That (a) left the misfire at d>=3.5 (9290 beard-oil d3.5 = 86826, +136% vs cjxl) AND
(b) created a NEW monotonicity cliff (9290 d3.0 = 44420 -> d3.5 = 86826, +95.5%) once
the sub-band below it was fixed. This change extends the p25 exclude to the main band.

CHANGE: the qf-seed gate now requires (m3 >= 24 OR mask1x1_p25 >= 95) on BOTH bands,
i.e. the p25 exclude applies to ALL LOW-COLOUR (m3 < 24) firing. HIGH-colour cells
(m3 >= 24) short-circuit the check, so their calibrated main-band behaviour is
byte-identical. Both paths edited: e5-7 resolved_adaptive_quant_qf_seed_scale_with_policy
(perceptual_tuning.rs) + e8+ buttloop auto_gate_fires (perceptual_loop.rs).

RESULT (verified, this table):
  - 9290 beard-oil (m3=23.4 LOW-colour PHOTO): FULLY MONOTONE e7 now
    (62790 -> 62533 -> 44420 -> 38671 -> 34345 -> 28572). d3.5 cliff GONE (86826 -> 38671).
  - SHIP low-colour screenshots UNCHANGED (lift still fires): imac_dark d4 = 223216
    (byte-size-identical to pre-change), d3.5 = 234494, d5 = 199102; imac_g3/terminal fire.
  - 9291 ingredients (m3=28.2 HIGH-colour PHOTO): STILL cliff at d3.5 (+87.6%) — CORRECTLY
    out of the low-colour scope; this is the residual HIGH-colour main-band misfire
